Root cause:
The root cause of the bug was the use of an unsigned variable `retval` in conditional checks that incorrectly included a comparison to less than zero (`retval < 0`). Since `retval` is an unsigned type, it can never be less than zero, leading to a smatch warning indicating that the condition is always false. The patch corrected this by removing the unnecessary comparison to zero, thus eliminating the warning and ensuring the logic correctly checks only for values greater than one.
